title start
kind: research
tags: business-plan legal-and-finance legal-finance-fair-use-and-news-quoting-limits
Legal finance fair use and news quoting limits
title end

section start
title start
Abstract
title end

paragraph start
Question: when may third party material be used without a licence. Method: a web search for United States Copyright Office guidance on fair use, read on 2026-10-29. Result: fair use is a doctrine that allows some unlicensed use, judged case by case on four factors with no fixed amount that is always safe, and non commercial use is not automatically fair. Limit: only United States law was searched, library guides stand in for the statute, and nothing here is legal advice.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Introduction
title end

paragraph start
The brand will use footage, images and music, so every third party item needs a licence, an owner permission or a recorded fair use reasoning. This page records the evidence on fair use.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Methods
title end

paragraph start
Searched the web for the Copyright Office fair use pages and read the office index page and several library guides that quote the statute and the office.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Results
title end

paragraph start
The Copyright Office describes its fair use index as a help for understanding past court decisions and says it is not a substitute for legal advice (copyright.gov, primary, checked 2026-10-29).
paragraph end

paragraph start
Library guides state that the statute names four factors: purpose and character of the use including whether it is commercial, nature of the work, amount used, and effect on the market (secondary).
paragraph end

paragraph start
A library guide reports the office as saying that no fixed percentage or number of words, lines or copies can be used without permission (Northeastern University library, secondary).
paragraph end

paragraph start
A university guide lists as a myth that all non commercial use is fair use, since all four factors must be weighed (University of Alabama libraries, secondary).
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Discussion
title end

paragraph start
Working rule for the plan: use only material the brand owns or holds a written licence for. Where fair use is the only basis, record the four factor reasoning and have a professional confirm it before publishing. Other countries use different rules and were not searched.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: choose the owner country, read the official statute and confirm the working rule with a professional
Not verified yet.
paragraph end

section end

